@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2553 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [762 x i8] }> <{ [762 x i8] c"# `exclusive_range_pattern`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#37854].\0A\0A\0A[#67264]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/67264\0A[#37854]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/37854\0A-----\0A\0AThe `exclusive_range_pattern` feature allows non-inclusive range\0Apatterns (`0..10`) to be used in appropriate pattern matching\0Acontexts. It also can be combined with `#![feature(half_open_range_patterns]`\0Ato be able to use RangeTo patterns (`..10`).\0A\0AIt also enabled RangeFrom patterns but that has since been\0Astabilized.\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(exclusive_range_pattern)]\0A    let x = 5;\0A    match x {\0A        0..10 => println!(\22single digit\22),\0A        10 => println!(\22ten isn't part of the above range\22),\0A        _ => println!(\22nor is everything else.\22)\0A    }\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
